  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "The official page is **PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython**: https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/\n\n1. **PEP 703 (canonical)** — https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/  \n   Sam Gross; sponsor Łukasz Langa. Status: Final (accepted; historical). Proposes `--disable-gil` so CPython can run without the GIL; ABI tag includes `t`. Created 9 Jan 2023; targeted at 3.13. Canonical free-threading docs are linked from the PEP. [web:8]\n\n2. **Steering Council acceptance** — https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075  \n   24 Oct 2023: SC accepts PEP 703 with a gradual three-phase rollout and the option to roll back. Suggests the term “free-threaded.” [web:4]\n\n3. **SC notice of intent to accept** — https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474  \n   28 Jul 2023: intent to accept; long-term goal of a single no-GIL build; experimental in 3.13, then supported but not default, then default later. [web:7]\n\n4. **PEP 779 – Criteria for supported status for free-threaded Python** — https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/  \n   Criteria for Phase II (officially supported, not default). Says 3.14 is the right time for Phase II; Phase III (default) is left to a future decision. [web:9]\n\n5. **Original PEP PR** — https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955  \n   `colesbury` PR “PEP 703: Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython,” merged into `python/peps` on 10 Jan 2023. [web:5]\n\n6. **Discussion thread** — https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606  \n   Early PEPs discussion (Jan 2023), including the `--disable-gil` configure-option naming. [web:6]\n\n7. **Overview (pydevtools)** — https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md  \n   Summary: `--disable-gil` build, biased refcounting, non-ABI-compatible free-threaded build, `t` wheel tag; experimental in 3.13, supported under PEP 779 in 3.14; default still has the GIL. [web:1]\n\n8. **Related: PEP 805 – Safe Parallel Python** — https://peps.python.org/pep-0805/  \n   Builds on PEP 703 and PEP 734; contrasts PEP 703’s shared-memory parallelism (and race conditions) with a safer sharing model. [web:10]",
